{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790461795,"nonce":"vqRzRi/L2vu5ye8VazbArprqxiU=","title":"Release archives carry no wasm runtime object","message":"`ash --build x.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1` links against\n`\u003cdir-of-ash\u003e/wasm32-wasip1/ash_runtime.o` (or `ASH_RUNTIME`). The release\ntarball from `scripts/package_release.sh` ships `ash`, `libash_std` and the\n`libhl` names, and no `wasm32-wasip1/` or `wasm32-wasip1-threads/` directory,\nso an installed `ash` refuses every wasm build with \"no ash_runtime.o for\nwasm32-wasip1 found\". `ash-wasm-run` is not shipped either.\n\nThe home page claimed nothing else is needed to build wasm; it now says the\nruntime is built once from a checkout, and website/wasm.html documents that.\n\nFix: build both runtime objects in release.yml (conformance.yml already\nfetches wasi-sdk-25 and caches the sysroot) and package them beside `ash`,\nplus `ash-wasm-run`.","files":null}]}